meta {
  name: 16 UpdateRegistry
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/registries
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "registry": [
      {
        "id": "{{registryId}}",
        "categories": [
          {
            "id": "{{categoryId}}",
            "sourceId": "{{categorySourceId}}",
            "entries": [
              {
                "idInSource": "234443",
                "sourceId": "System A",
                "name": "Loop 106 (renamed)"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 204", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(204);
  });
}

docs {
  §3.1.3 is a snapshot replace: every non-primary-key attribute of each supplied
  object is set from the supplied data, so an omitted attribute is CLEARED.
  Here sourceOwnerId was "Refinery-01" on the seed and is absent above, so it
  becomes null.

  Two interpretations this implementation makes, both stated in the conformance
  document:

  - Children that are not supplied are left alone. A separate Delete family
    exists, so treating an omitted Entry as a removal would make partial
    updates impossible.
  - CIRID is preserved when omitted rather than cleared, because §3.1.4 is a
    dedicated operation for it and §3.1.2 treats it as server-managed state.
}
